#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:5
msgid "UFS Emulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:7
msgid ""
"QEMU emulates a Universal Flash Storage (UFS) host controller and the "
"logical units behind it. The host controller follows the UFSHCI register "
"interface and reports UFS version 4.1 to the guest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:11
msgid "Two devices are involved:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:13
msgid "``ufs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:14
msgid ""
"The host controller on the PCI bus. A ``sysbus-ufs`` variant exists for "
"boards that place the controller on the system bus; it cannot be created "
"with ``-device``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:18
msgid "``ufs-lu``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:19
msgid ""
"A logical unit attached to a host controller through ``bus=``. Each logical "
"unit is backed by a block device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:22
msgid ""
"The well-known logical units (REPORT LUNS, UFS Device, Boot and RPMB) are "
"created by the host controller and need no configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:26
msgid "Adding a UFS Device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:28
msgid ""
"The following adds a host controller with MCQ enabled and one logical unit "
"backed by ``ufs.img``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:31
msgid ""
"-drive file=ufs.img,if=none,id=lu0,format=raw \\\n"
"-device ufs,id=ufs0,serial=0001,mcq=on \\\n"
"-device ufs-lu,drive=lu0,bus=ufs0,lun=0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:37
msgid ""
"Add more ``ufs-lu`` devices with different ``lun`` values to create more "
"logical units. On top of the architecture defconfig, a Linux guest needs "
"``CONFIG_SCSI_UFSHCD``, ``CONFIG_SCSI_UFSHCD_PCI`` and "
"``CONFIG_BLK_DEV_SD``; each logical unit then appears as a SCSI disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:43
msgid "Host Controller Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:45
msgid "``serial``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:46
msgid ""
"Serial number string. It is accepted but not reported to the guest yet; the "
"serial number string descriptor reads back empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:49
msgid "``nutrs`` (default 32, maximum 32)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:50
msgid "Number of UTP transfer request slots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:52
msgid "``nutmrs`` (default 8, maximum 8)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:53
msgid ""
"Number of UTP task management request slots advertised to the guest. Task "
"management requests are not processed yet (see Limitations)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:56
msgid "``mcq`` (default off)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:57
msgid ""
"Advertise Multi-Circular Queue (MCQ) support. When off, the guest uses the "
"single doorbell transfer request list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:60
msgid "``mcq-maxq`` (default 2, maximum 31)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:61
msgid "Number of MCQ submission and completion queue pairs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:63
msgid "``wb-max-size``, ``wb-min-size`` (default 0x400 and 0x100)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:64
msgid ""
"Maximum and minimum WriteBooster buffer size, in allocation units. ``wb-min-"
"size`` must not exceed ``wb-max-size``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:68
msgid "Logical Unit Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:70
msgid "``drive``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:71
msgid "Backing block device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:73
msgid "``lun`` (default 0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:74
msgid ""
"Logical unit number, 0 to 31. A host controller accepts up to 32 logical "
"units."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:78
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:80
msgid ""
"UniPro and M-PHY are not modelled. Only the UIC commands needed for link "
"startup, DME attribute access and hibernation are handled; DME reads return "
"fixed values, and DME writes, power mode changes and hibernation do not "
"change any link state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:84
msgid ""
"UTP task management requests are not processed, so a guest that tries to "
"abort a command or reset a logical unit gets no completion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:86
msgid ""
"The Boot and RPMB well-known logical units only answer basic SCSI commands "
"such as INQUIRY; boot and RPMB data access are not emulated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/devices/ufs.rst:88
msgid "The device cannot be migrated."
msgstr ""
